  "question": {
    "text": "In <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;the equation of the internal angle bisector of angle <math><mi>Q</mi></math> is <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></math> and the equation of side <math><mi>P</mi><mi>R</mi></math> is <math><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo></math> If coordinates of <math><mi>P</mi></math> are <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>3,2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math><mn>2</mn><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo></math> then the coordinates of <math><mi>Q</mi></math> are"
  },
